      - title: Menu Text
        value: 
        type: 0
        typeString: 
      - title: Dialogue Text
        value: "I was once called Hadassah\u2014unknown, unseen. Yet I was taken
          into the king\u2019s house\u2026 and made queen. A crown upon my head,
          yet fear within my heart.\nI concealed my kindred and my people, dwelling
          in quietness, unsure of mine own place, ever beholding, and ever in fear.\n\nThen
          went there forth a decree, that my people should be utterly destroyed.
          Fear gat hold upon me, for I alone stood near unto the throne; yet might
          I not draw nigh unto the king, except I should adventure my life.\n\nI
          tarried in my spirit. I was of a doubtful heart. I feared the silence,
          and the distance, and the great price of the way.\n\nNevertheless, a word
          moved within my soul\u2014what if I were set in this place for this very
          hour?\n\nTherefore I purposed to go in, though I trembled; I stepped forth
          into peril, trusting that I was not forgotten of the Most High. The God
          of mine people\nThe Queen: \u201CWho knoweth whether thou art come to the
          kingdom for such a time as this?\u201D \u2014 Esther 4:14"
        type: 0
        typeString: 
